ated for all  further points so at the end we have one  yellow cluster  one red cluster and one green cluster  then all points are initially assigned  to a cluster  we have defined the number of clusters  we have assigned  the cluster centroid randomly in this  space and we have assigned each of the  point  to one cluster now we can calculate the  center of each  cluster so we can calculate the center  of the clusters  for the green points for the yellow  points and  for the red points the center of each  cluster  is calculated these centers are the new  sentries for the clusters that means  that we simply shift  the centroids into the cluster center  so the cluster centroids are moved to  the cluster  centers in the fifth step we assign  the points to the new clusters since the  sentries can now be located at a  different point  each point is again assigned to the  cluster that is closer to it  this was our initial condition now  the center of the cluster is moved and  for sure now we can assign again  the points to the cluster which is  closest to them  and this will be our new cluster  now we have finished with all steps and  we do  one final step we will repeat step 4  and 5. now steps 4 and 5 are repeated  until the cluster distribution does not  change anymore calculate the center of  each cluster  assign cluster centroid to the center  and assign the points to the new cluster  if the clusters do not change in one  iteration  the procedure is over and in the final  step we move the clusters  to the new center in this step  the cluster will not change anymore in a  new iteration  a big disadvantage of the k-means method  is  that the final results depends very much  on which initial clusters was used  to take this into account the whole  procedure  is carried out several times different  randomly  chosen starting points are then used for  each of the calculations  since the cluster is used which has the  smallest  sum of distances between the cluster  center  and the points each time we use  different starting points it could be  that the outcome is different  so we do the whole cluster analysis  several times in  order to get the best possible result  data tab  for example do the cluster analysis 10  times  with 10 different randomly chosen  starting points  and then at the end select the best  cluster so  what is the optimal cluster number with  each  new cluster the summed distance in the  clusters become  smaller and smaller so if we had a look  at this picture where we have two  clusters and  this picture where we have three  clusters for sure  these three clusters does fit the data  better  than these two clusters and the distance  between the points and the clusters is  in this case higher than  in this case if there are as many  clusters as points  for sure the outcome will be zero now  the question is  how many clusters should be used to  answer this question  we use the album method again with  each additional cluster the summed  distance between the points  and the cluster center becomes smaller  and smaller  however there is a cluster number from  which each  additional cluster reduces the sum  distance only  slightly this point is used as a number  of the cluster so if we have a  look at this plot we can see that  there's a  big gap between cluster number one and  two  and there's also a big gap between the  number of clusters two  and three but there's only a small  gap between number of clusters three  and four so in this case we will select  three as a number of clusters and now  i'd like to show you how we can  easily calculate a k-mean cluster  analysis  online with data tab to do this please  visit  datatab.net and click on statistics  calculator  because we want to calculate a cluster  analysis simply select  cluster in order to use your own data  you can  clear the table and then copy your own  data into this table  i will simply use example data so  we want to calculate a k-means cluster  analysis  and let's say we want to analysis  salary and age now we can define  the number of clusters and  if we enter the number of clusters data  tab  will calculate the whole method  so here we can see the three clusters  with the centuries and you can  here we can see the elbow methods in  this case  it will indicate us that we can use two  as a number of clusters we have select  three  so we can change it in order to get the  right number of clusters  but let's go through the results first  so  here we can see how many points are  assigned to the different clusters  so and here we get the plot with the  different clusters  here we can see one cluster here we can  see one cluster  and here we can see one cluster and  further we get a table where we allocate  each point to a cluster  so but now if we choose two  as the number of clusters and we get  the new results and we can see here  in this plot that we have one cluster  here and  one cluster here and we can see that the  two clusters  fits the data quite well thanks for  watching this video  i hope you liked it and see you soon bye
 

